  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question 6
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: '6. The concentration of Na<sub>2</sub>S<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>
    solution should be more than that of KI solution.

'
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: 'The liberated iodine in the reaction must consume all the thiosulphate
    ions. The increased

    concentration of iodine forms a complex with the starch,
    resulting in blue colouration. Thus, the

    concentration of Na<sub>2</sub>S<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>
    solution should be less than that of KI solution.'
  options:
  - True
  - False
  correctOptionIndex: 1
